    # Only when / Only after / Only by / Not until / Not only (86-110)
    ("Only when she removed her sunglasses ______ who she actually was.", ["we recognized", "did we recognize", "had we recognized", "we did recognize"], 1, "U 'Only when...' je první věta normální a inverze nastává až ve DRUHÉ (hlavní) větě: 'did we recognize'.", "Chyták: U 'Only when/after/if' neinvertuj první větu!"),
    ("Not until midnight ______ return from the emergency summit.", ["the envoy did", "did the envoy", "had the envoy", "was the envoy"], 1, "Po 'Not until + čas' se invertuje hlavní věta: 'did the envoy return'.", "Not until midnight = Až o půlnoci."),
    ("Only by streamlining our logistics ______ remain competitive globally.", ["we can", "can we", "do we can", "we will"], 1, "'Only by + -ing' vyžaduje inverzi v hlavní větě: 'can we remain'.", "Streamline = zefektivnit / zeštíhlit."),
    ("Not only ______ win the gold medal, but she also shattered the world record.", ["she did", "did she", "was she", "had she"], 1, "Vazba 'Not only + inverze, but + normální slovosled': 'Not only did she win...'.", "Druhá část za 'but' už inverzi nemá!"),
    ("Only after reviewing the security footage ______ what had actually transpired.", ["the detective knew", "did the detective know", "had the detective known", "was the detective knowing"], 1, "'Only after + -ing' ➔ inverze v hlavní větě: 'did the detective know'.", "Transpire = vyjít najevo / stát se."),
    ("Not until the final paragraph ______ reveal the true identity of the narrator.", ["the author does", "does the author", "the author did", "is the author"], 1, "Přítomný čas vypravěče (historický prézens): 'does the author reveal'.", "Po 'does' je sloveso bez -s (reveal)."),
